{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup for the `option-picker` atom — the single source of truth for
  what this atom renders. Two callers, and they must not drift:
    - blocks/dm-option-picker.liquid  — as a Shopify theme block (shallow)
    - the inline emitter        — as {% render %} inside a parent's
                                  dm_inline setting, when nesting would
                                  otherwise blow Shopify's depth cap of 8

  Params are flat (not a settings object) because Liquid has no object
  literal, so the inline emitter can only pass key: value pairs.
  Slot content arrives PRE-RENDERED as string params (children, …): a
  snippet can never run `content_for`, so the caller captures it.

  No defaults here, deliberately. A {% schema %} `default` is an EDITOR
  seed — it populates the JSON when a merchant adds a block — NOT a
  render-time fallback. Our templates are machine-generated, so a setting
  the emitter omits (`omitValue`) is simply absent and reads blank. Both
  callers take their values from that same emitter map, so re-declaring
  defaults here would invent attributes that never render today.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  DM Option Picker — storefront mirror.

  Renders an outer flex container with one `[data-option-picker-item]`
  item per Shopify option value, multiplying the merchant-authored item
  template via placeholder replacement.

  Same captured-template + placeholder-replace pattern as
  dm-dropdown.liquid. Placeholders inside the item template:
    __DM_V_VALUE__         option value ("Red", "L")
    __DM_V_OPTION_NAME__   option name from the product ("Color")
    __DM_V_PRODUCT_ID__    product id
    __DM_V_ACTIVE__        "true" / "false" — set on the variant initially
                           matching the storefront's selected variant
    __DM_V_AVAILABLE__     "true" / "false"
    __DM_V_TITLE__         full variant title ("Red / L")
    __DM_V_PRICE__         money-formatted price
    __DM_V_COMPARE_AT__    money-formatted compare-at-price (or empty)
    __DM_V_IMAGE_SRC__     featured image URL (or empty)

  Click handling is centralized in `dm-option-picker.js`. The card-level
  `--dm-swatch` slot comes from the `swatches` setting — per-value colours
  resolved at publish (merchant override, else our name guess) so the
  storefront paints exactly what the canvas did. Absent setting (a theme
  published before this shipped) falls back to reading the value itself as a
  CSS colour name, which is what this always did.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign p = closest.product | default: product -%}

{%- capture outer_inline -%}{{ custom_styles_inline }}{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Per-item surface — the transpiler hoisted the item root atom (Card, or a
  bare ColorSwatch for naked swatch pickers) into `item_attrs` +
  `item_inline` (pre-rendered flat strings, same pattern as
  custom_styles_attrs/_inline). The wrapper div below IS that root on the
  storefront — it carries `data-atom-type="card"` /
  `data-atom-type="color-swatch"` via item_attrs, so theme CSS styles it
  exactly like the editor's stamped element. (A swatch root publishes with
  zero inner blocks — the wrapper renders as the swatch itself.)

  Hover + selected are derived in CSS, not emitted here.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Capture the item template once at the top — Shopify allows only one
  `content_for 'blocks'` per template. Reuse for the no-product fallback
  AND the per-value duplication loop below.
{%- endcomment -%}


{%- comment -%}
  Shared option resolution + outer-attr surface — used by every branch
  below (manual / no-product clone / clone loop) so they can't drift.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign option_key = option | default: 'option_1'
  assign option_idx = 0
  if option_key == 'option_2'
    assign option_idx = 1
  elsif option_key == 'option_3'
    assign option_idx = 2
  endif
  assign option = nil
  if p != blank
    assign option = p.options_with_values[option_idx]
  endif
-%}
{%- capture outer_attrs -%}
    {% if direction != blank %}data-flex-direction="{{ direction }}"{% endif %}
    {% if direction_sm != blank %}data-flex-direction-sm="{{ direction_sm }}"{% endif %}
    {% if gap != blank %}data-flex-gap="{{ gap }}"{% endif %}
    {% if gap_sm != blank %}data-flex-gap-sm="{{ gap_sm }}"{% endif %}
    {% if align != blank %}data-flex-align="{{ align }}"{% endif %}
    {% if align_sm != blank %}data-flex-align-sm="{{ align_sm }}"{% endif %}
    {% if justify != blank %}data-flex-justify="{{ justify }}"{% endif %}
    {% if justify_sm != blank %}data-flex-justify-sm="{{ justify_sm }}"{% endif %}
    {% if wrap != blank %}data-flex-wrap="{{ wrap }}"{% endif %}
    {% if wrap_sm != blank %}data-flex-wrap-sm="{{ wrap_sm }}"{% endif %}
    {{ custom_styles_attrs }}
    {% if outer_inline != blank %}style="{{ outer_inline }}"{% endif %}
    {{ shopify_attributes }}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Unresolvable-token fallback. The clone loop below substitutes every
  `__DM_V_*` per option value, but the two branches that render
  `item_template` ONCE have no variant to resolve against:
    - manual mode — each bound Card substituted its own tokens already
      (dm-card.liquid), so anything still here had no card to resolve it;
    - no product context (home page, blog, any non-product template) —
      nothing resolves.
  Either way the token is dead, and a dead token must render as empty, not
  as `__DM_V_PRICE__` on a live storefront. Mirrors dm-atom-text.liquid,
  which already blanks its `__DM_P_*` tokens whether or not `p` exists.
  A separate variable — the clone loop re-reads `item_template` per value.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # Only the two once-rendered branches need it — the clone loop below
  # re-reads `item_template` and substitutes for real.
  if mode == 'manual' or p == blank
    assign item_fallback = item_template
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_VALUE__', ''
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_OPTION_NAME__', ''
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_PRODUCT_ID__', ''
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_ACTIVE__', 'false'
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_AVAILABLE__', 'false'
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_TITLE__', ''
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_PRICE__', ''
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_COMPARE_AT__', ''
    assign item_fallback = item_fallback | replace: '__DM_V_IMAGE_SRC__', ''
  endif
-%}

{%- if mode == 'manual' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Manual mode — no multiplication, no placeholder replacement. The
    authored child blocks render as-is; each bound Card self-stamps its
    selection attrs via dm-card.liquid + the dm-picker-item-attrs snippet.
    dm-option-picker.js works unchanged (attribute-driven).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <dm-option-picker data-atom-type="option-picker"
    {% if p != blank %}data-dm-product-id="{{ p.id }}"{% endif %}
    {% if option != blank %}data-option-name="{{ option.name | escape }}"{% endif %}
    {{ outer_attrs }}
  >
    {{ item_fallback }}
  </dm-option-picker>
{%- elsif p == blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    No product context — render the authored template once inside a single
    card wrapper so merchants can preview the layout on non-product pages.
    Click handler no-ops without `data-dm-product-id`.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <dm-option-picker data-atom-type="option-picker"
    {{ outer_attrs }}
  >
    <div
      data-option-picker-item
      data-active="false"
      {{ item_attrs }}
      {% if item_inline != blank %}style="{{ item_inline }}"{% endif %}
    >
      {{ item_fallback }}
    </div>
  </dm-option-picker>
{%- else -%}
  <dm-option-picker data-atom-type="option-picker"
    data-dm-product-id="{{ p.id }}"
    {% if option != blank %}data-option-name="{{ option.name | escape }}"{% endif %}
    {{ outer_attrs }}
  >
    {%- if option == blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}Selected option doesn't exist on this product.{%- endcomment -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign selected_value = option.selected_value -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Resolved swatch colours, baked at publish as `Value=#hex|Value=#hex`
        (see `serializeSwatchesForShopify`). Split once here rather than per
        value. When the setting is absent — a theme published before this
        shipped — every lookup misses and the fallback below keeps the old
        behaviour, so an old theme renders exactly as it did.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign swatch_pairs = swatches | split: '|' -%}
      {%- for value in option.values -%}
        {%- liquid
          # Colour for THIS value: the baked entry, else the value itself read
          # as a CSS colour name — which is all this ever had, and is why
          # "Brown" painted CSS brown (#A52A2A) rather than ours.
          assign swatch_color = value
          for pair in swatch_pairs
            assign kv = pair | split: '='
            if kv[0] == value
              assign swatch_color = kv[1]
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign matching_variant = nil
          for v in p.variants
            if option_idx == 0 and v.option1 == value
              assign matching_variant = v
              break
            elsif option_idx == 1 and v.option2 == value
              assign matching_variant = v
              break
            elsif option_idx == 2 and v.option3 == value
              assign matching_variant = v
              break
            endif
          endfor

          assign is_active = 'false'
          if selected_value == value
            assign is_active = 'true'
          endif

          # Available when ANY variant at this option-value is in stock —
          # mirrors the editor logic. Multi-option products may have some
          # combinations sold-out without disabling the whole value.
          assign is_available = 'false'
          for v in p.variants
            if option_idx == 0 and v.option1 == value and v.available
              assign is_available = 'true'
              break
            elsif option_idx == 1 and v.option2 == value and v.available
              assign is_available = 'true'
              break
            elsif option_idx == 2 and v.option3 == value and v.available
              assign is_available = 'true'
              break
            endif
          endfor

          assign price_str = ''
          assign compare_str = ''
          assign image_src = ''
          assign variant_title = value
          if matching_variant != nil
            assign price_str = matching_variant.price | money
            if matching_variant.compare_at_price > matching_variant.price
              assign compare_str = matching_variant.compare_at_price | money
            endif
            if matching_variant.featured_media != nil
              assign image_src = matching_variant.featured_media | img_url: '600x'
            endif
            assign variant_title = matching_variant.title
          endif

          assign item_html = item_template
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_VALUE__', value
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_OPTION_NAME__', option.name
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_PRODUCT_ID__', p.id
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_ACTIVE__', is_active
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_AVAILABLE__', is_available
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_TITLE__', variant_title
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_PRICE__', price_str
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_COMPARE_AT__', compare_str
          assign item_html = item_html | replace: '__DM_V_IMAGE_SRC__', image_src
        -%}
        {%- capture item_style -%}{{ item_inline }}--dm-swatch: {{ swatch_color }};{%- endcapture -%}
        <div
          data-option-picker-item
          data-variant-value="{{ value | escape }}"
          data-variant-option-name="{{ option.name | escape }}"
          data-dm-product-id="{{ p.id }}"
          data-active="{{ is_active }}"
          data-variant-available="{{ is_available }}"
          {{ item_attrs }}
          style="{{ item_style }}"
        >
          {{ item_html }}
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </dm-option-picker>
{%- endif -%}
